    {
      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <climits>\n#include <omp.h>\n\nint main() {\n    int n, s;\n    std::cin >> n >> s;\n    \n    // Read matrix into flat array (row-major)\n    std::vector<int> mat(n * n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            scanf(\"%d\", &mat[i * n + j]);\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Prefix sum array: dimensions (n+1) x (n+1), initialized to zero\n    int psize = n + 1;\n    std::vector<long long> pref(psize * psize, 0);\n\n    // Pass 1: row-wise prefix sums (independent per row)\n    #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static) if(n > 100)\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        int base_row = i * n;\n        int base_pref = (i + 1) * psize;\n        long long cum = 0;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            cum += mat[base_row + j];\n            pref[base_pref + (j + 1)] = cum;\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Pass 2: column-wise accumulation to obtain full 2D prefix sums\n    #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static) if(n > 100)\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n        int col = j + 1;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n            pref[(i + 1) * psize + col] += pref[i * psize + col];\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Evaluate all SxS submatrices in O(1) each using the prefix sum array\n    long long mxSum = LLONG_MIN;\n    #pragma omp parallel for collapse(2) reduction(max:mxSum)\n    for (int i = 0; i <= n - s; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j <= n - s; ++j) {\n            int i1 = i, j1 = j;\n            int i2 = i + s, j2 = j + s;\n            long long sum = pref[i2 * psize + j2] \n                           - pref[i1 * psize + j2] \n                           - pref[i2 * psize + j1] \n                           + pref[i1 * psize + j1];\n            if (sum > mxSum) mxSum = sum;\n        }\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", mxSum);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Compute 2D prefix sum using two parallel passes (row-wise then column-wise) on a flat array, eliminating intermediate storage. Evaluate all SxS submatrix sums in O(1) each with OpenMP collapse and reduction(max). Use long long for safety and potential NEON vectorization.",
  "notes": "This approach reduces memory footprint compared to previous integral-image implementations by reusing a single prefix sum array. The two-pass method allows full parallelism in each pass, and the final evaluation loop is collapsed for better load balancing.",
